  "note": "Eighty seconds and the tin's in my tray, so I'm not sliding Phil his ordinary card. I keep the handoff reserved, read the line meter, and let the wire weather sit. The flat's blocking the acoustic window anyway—no one sees me pull the old ident off the shelf. This is my drawer, my broadcast, and the tape still says Mercury. I'll cue it clean before the lamp hits zero."
